A gas-equivalent reading is not a mixture analysis (@gas-gauge-mixtures: 0, is #chapter, #part-of @industrial-gases-and-vacuum, #source "../sources/Ionization-Gauge-Calibration-Fedchak.lingua#r_18KG5KWT64MPYQ4D47V1T99CKW", #source "../sources/Total-and-Partial-Pressure-Jousten.lingua#r_7SH9NGBWVVK5YN24S2VZPTW45M", #industrial-gases-and-vacuum "The-gauge-can-change-the-gas-at-its-own-inlet.lingua#r_1KSEFRSR9NJ56SGBFVWG6ZAXPC") { r_2NZ4WVFZ4F5PZ63NHAKCH3C1M1
**Read:** [Calibration of ionization vacuum gauges — Fedchak and colleagues](../sources/Ionization-Gauge-Calibration-Fedchak.lingua#r_18KG5KWT64MPYQ4D47V1T99CKW), relative gas sensitivity; [Total and Partial Pressure Measurement — Karl Jousten](../sources/Total-and-Partial-Pressure-Jousten.lingua#r_7SH9NGBWVVK5YN24S2VZPTW45M), calibration and partial-pressure discussion.

In a linear additive ion-current model, Ic=IeΣKi pi. If a controller divides by KN2Ie, the displayed nitrogen-equivalent pressure is pN2eq=Σsi pi, where si=Ki/KN2. The actual total pressure is Σpi. They coincide only for particular compositions or sensitivities.

As a hypothetical two-gas example, let partial pressures be 2×10⁻⁶ and 3×10⁻⁶ Pa and relative sensitivities 1 and 0.4. The equivalent reading is 3.2×10⁻⁶ Pa while the total is 5×10⁻⁶ Pa. One number cannot determine both unknown partial pressures. A pure-gas correction cannot solve an unidentified mixture.

Sensitivity factors can depend on instrument condition and pressure. Ion fragmentation, multiply charged ions and additional backgrounds complicate other instruments too. State the gas basis with a reported equivalent indication and preserve the uncertainty of any conversion.

**Work:** Find several nonnegative mixtures that produce the same hypothetical equivalent reading. Identify what additional independent observation would make the mixture inference possible, then test whether that observation has a sufficiently different response to the components.

**Return:** [Industrial gases, vacuum and high-purity supplies — from molecules to useful service](../Industrial-gases-and-vacuum.lingua#r_3GHQJEYMYEN6JDKSF4PPJ403RF).
